items.body:
Placing 48 shots back to back at beat times (`at: n × 0.4296 s`) with computed source ranges left a one-frame gap (32.633–32.667 s) where a clip's rounded end fell short of the next one's rounded start. It was only found by reading the timeline, and needed a trim to close.

Wanted, one of:
- `place {…, at: "after_previous"}` (or `at: {after: clip_id}`), which butts a clip against the one before it on that track;
- `place` with `length_frames`/`to` and the out snapped to the next clip's in when they are within half a frame;
- a warning in the apply reply when a place leaves a gap or overlap under a frame on its track.
